postvec (${POSTVEC_VERSION}-${PACKAGE_RELEASE}) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `postvec model` and `postvec provider` no longer need a local
    postvec-enabled database. With no cluster running postvec they manage
    directory POSTVEC_PATH or /opt/postvec
  * One engine-root variable: postvec-server reads POSTVEC_PATH, like the
    CLI. POSTVEC_SERVER_ROOT is removed and POSTVEC_SERVER_PROVIDERS_PATH
    is replaced by POSTVEC_PROVIDERS_PATH
  * `model pull` creates models/ inside an existing root. A fresh root lists
    as empty and can be previewed with --dry-run. `model ls --available
    --path DIR` shows what is installed in that root
  * postvec-server image: the entrypoint skips TLS setup for CLI and admin
    commands, accepts --ssl-cert=/--ssl-key= and a case-insensitive
    POSTVEC_SERVER_INSECURE, and refuses a half-present certificate pair
    instead of replacing it

 -- ${MAINTAINER}  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:55:42 +0000

postvec (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Converters L2-normalize their input vectors before conversion
    (executor.params.normalize_input - default on) matching the hosted
    API (converters trained on unit-length embeddings)
  * Registry fixes: converters from API-only embedding spaces (OpenAI, Cohere,
    Gemini, Titan, Mistral) install cleanly

 -- ${MAINTAINER}  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 15:28:01 +0000

